.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-SCHEMA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-schema
.Nd pin and check the schema of CSV files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis schema infer
.Op Fl d | Fl -delim Ar c
.Op Fl -no-header
.Op Fl -ranges
.Op Fl -put
.Ar dir file ...
.Nm noqtis schema check
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Ar dir
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Cm infer
reads each CSV
.Ar file
in
.Ar dir
(RFC 4180: a delimiter byte, LF or CRLF line ends, quoted fields with
.Ql \&""
for a quote and line breaks kept inside, a UTF-8 byte order mark
skipped) and prints its schema, a
.Cm schemas
element of the data record
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5 ,
as one line of JSON: the columns in order with their names, the
narrowest type every value fits
.Po
.Ql bool
.Pq true, false, TRUE, FALSE, True, False ,
.Ql int
(an optional minus and at most 18 digits, no leading zero, so codes
such as
.Ql 007
stay text),
.Ql real
(a JSON number),
.Ql date
.Pq Ql YYYY-MM-DD ,
else
.Ql text
.Pc ,
whether each has missing values (the empty field and
.Ql NA ) ,
and the number of rows, pinned as its minimum and maximum.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d , Fl -delim Ar c
the delimiter, one byte (default
.Ql \&, ;
.Cm tab
for a tab)
.It Fl -no-header
the first line is data; the columns are named V1, V2, ...
.It Fl -ranges
pin each number and date column's smallest and largest value too
.It Fl -put
record the schemas in the data record instead of printing them,
replacing any for the same file
.El
.Pp
.Cm check
checks the files against the schemas the record pins (every schema, or
those of the files named): the header against the column names, the
number of fields of each line, each value against its column's type,
missing-value codes,
.Cm nulls ,
.Cm min ,
.Cm max
and
.Cm set ,
the row count, and each rule
.Po
.Ql unique ,
.Ql notnull ,
.Ql range ,
.Ql set ,
.Ql incr ,
.Ql complete ,
.Ql distinct ,
.Ql rows ,
.Ql cols
.Pc .
A file that is not CSV fails its row with the line where it stops
being CSV.
It shows the first ten problems of a file and how many there are in
all, one row per rule, and on standard error what to do.
.Cm noqtis data check
runs the same checks with the rest of the record.
Edit a schema, or add rules, with
.Cm noqtis data put Ar dir Cm schemas Ar file .
.Pp
Limits: a field of at most 1 MiB, a line of at most 16 MiB and 16,384
fields; a
.Ql unique
or
.Ql distinct
rule holds at most 2^25 distinct values.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
success; for
.Cm check ,
every check passed
.It 1
.Cm check :
a check failed
.It 2
a usage or file error, a file that is not CSV
.Pq Cm infer ,
or a folder with no schema to check
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis schema infer --put results data/a.csv
$ noqtis schema check results
      check   detail
ok    schema  data/a.csv: 3 rows, 4 columns as the schema says
results: OK (1 checks passed)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr nqdinfer 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
